<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernard VI of Armagnac</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1319</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernard VI was count of Armagnac and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezensac">Fezensac</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Through his marriage to Cécile, daughter and heiress of Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-count-of-rodez">Henry II of Rodez</a>, he gained the county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rodez">Rodez</a> in 1302, which became one of the chief holdings of the house of Armagnac. The union greatly increased the family's power in southern France.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernard-vi-of-armagnac.jpg" alt="Bernard VI of Armagnac" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paul Laplagne Barris · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bernard_VI_d%27Armagnac.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
